validator_title = A validator that can say no
validator_text = Five checks run on every floor: connectivity, clearances, doors, corridor geometry, and the distance from entrance to stairs. A floor that fails is thrown away and dug again from a derived seed.
validator_caption = Seed { $seed }, first draw, rejected:
rejected_figure_label = A floor the validator rejected, because its stairs are too close to the entrance.
descent_title = How a floor is dug
descent_seed_title = A seed
descent_seed_text = One number and a set of parameters feed a small deterministic generator. The same inputs give the same floor, on the desktop or in the browser.
descent_rooms_title = Chambers
descent_rooms_text = Rooms are fitted block by block, shape by shape, with the weights and caps you set.
descent_tunnels_title = Tunnels
descent_tunnels_text = Doors first, then corridors with at most a few bends, branching into T and X junctions, always a clear distance from the rooms they do not join.
descent_check_title = Daylight
descent_check_text = The validator opens the door and looks. Only a floor that passes every check is handed back.
